-- S1 in the OTHER direction: a plain (auto-resume) arm that binds one binder
-- too many. Pre-retrofit, the extra binder silently promoted the arm to the
-- continuation-taking reading; the two readings were distinguished only by
-- counting, so neither mistake could be reported. A plain arm now promises
-- EXACTLY the operation's arity, and E-ARITY reports the surplus.
--
-- Together with 56-once-arity-collapse this pins the collapse as loud in both
-- directions, which is what makes the declared clause kind worth its keyword.
--
-- codemod: skip
-- This file HOLDS the mis-shaped arm on purpose. A plain arm binding arity + 1
-- is exactly the shape the migration promotes to `once`, so without this marker
-- a re-run of tools/Codemod.hs would silently repair the fixture and delete the
-- regression it exists to pin.
module Main
import Base

effect Call = { call : (U64 -> U64) -> U64 }

useCall : () -> U64 with Call
useCall u = Call.call (\n -> n + 1)

main : U64
main =
  with { Call.call f k -> k (f 41) }
  useCall ()
